==Notes==

*Requires [[Hordes of the Underdark]].
*The duration is the barbarian's constitution modifier (before the rage) plus 11 rounds.
*This feat's prerequisites require barbarian level 20. (This is when the feat called "greater rage (6x per day)" is acquired.)
* ''Mighty rage'' does not replace ''greater rage''; it is a separate ability that can be activated three times per day. However, ''mighty rage'' has no effect if activated while ''greater rage'' in effect. (The reverse works though &ndash; one can use ''mighty rage'' then ''barbarian rage'' to get the effects of both.)
*Unlike normal rage, mighty rage does not give an [[armor class]] penalty.
*Like a normal rage, mighty rage can be improved by [[terrifying rage]] and [[thundering rage]] feats.
*[[Ability]] bonuses are [[ability cap|capped]] at +12, so a barbarian with bonuses from [[item]]s, [[spell]]s or [[potion]]s might not gain the full ability bonuses from ''mighty rage''.
*This feat can only be selected when leveling as a [[barbarian]].

==Custom content notes==
*A custom class must have this feat in their feat list, or that class will not be able to select it as a general feat.
* ''script:'' <code>X2_S2_MghtyRage</code>
